Glide64mk2: RenderHeight, the height the game is drawn at.

The plugin draws straight to the window, at its size. With RenderHeight
(Video-Glide64mk2, 0: the window's) below the window's height, it draws in a
framebuffer object of that height and of the window's shape, whose two colour
attachments stand for GL_BACK and GL_FRONT, and scales each frame to the
window (linear). The window keeps the size of Video-General; anti-aliasing
is off in this mode (the framebuffer has no samples). OpenGL ES builds
ignore it.

